---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
import { url } from "../lib/url";
const { links } = site;
---

<Base title="About">
  <section class="wrap page prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>{site.intro}</p>

    <h2>How I build</h2>
    <p class="todo">
      Draft for you to rewrite in your own words before publishing. Course policy requires disclosing AI tool use, and
      this section should say exactly what you did. Keep only what you can explain in an interview.
    </p>
    <p>
      I write a spec and the tests first, and I direct AI coding agents through the implementation. I review every change,
      and nothing ships until it passes black-box tests that drive the system the way the course autograder does, over its
      TCP/JSON protocol. The course then checks that I understand the code: I repair deliberately broken copies of my own
      projects without AI tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      {links.email && <li><a href={`mailto:${links.email}`}>{links.email}</a></li>}
      {links.github && <li><a href={links.github}>GitHub</a></li>}
      {links.linkedin && <li><a href={links.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a></li>}
      {links.cv && <li><a href={url(links.cv)}>CV (PDF)</a></li>}
      {!links.email && !links.github && !links.linkedin && !links.cv && (
        <li class="muted">TODO: add links in <code>src/site.ts</code>.</li>
      )}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 40px; }
</style>
